docs/papers172_176_sequence/scouting/fresh_geometry_automata/SCOUT_AND_KILL_LEDGER.md:9:| `D01_ORT` | Set partitions of `[n]`.  Replace each element's block label by its zero-based occurrence rank within that old block, then canonicalise as an RGS. | Every partition through `n=9` (21,147 at the last rank). `T^3=T`; image sizes `1,2,4,10,26,76,232,764,2620`; no fixed point for `n>=2`; all image states are 2-cycles and every other state has depth one. | For target layers `B_j`, adjacent order-restricted injections give `prod_(j,i)(#{y in B_j:y<x_i}-i+1)`; the verifier also checks a gap-marked injection permanent target by target through `n=8`. | **`KILL_DIRECT_OWNER`.** Prasad--Ram Definition 2.1 is the literal set-partition-to-tableau map; Theorem 2.8 owns its fibre and Theorem 3.4 a stronger natural marked fibre.  Tableau transpose gives the residual clock for free. |
docs/papers172_176_sequence/scouting/fresh_geometry_automata/SCOUT_AND_KILL_LEDGER.md:11:| `D03_FSP` | Endofunctions `f:[n]->[n]`.  In each old fibre, cyclically send its increasingly ordered elements to their successors. | All `n^n` functions through `n=6`.  Image size is `Bell(n)`; identity is the sole recurrent state; the `n!-1` nonidentity bijections have depth one and all `n^n-n!` nonbijections depth two. | A canonical target with `k` increasing cycles has `(n)_k` parents.  A fixed-point-marked polynomial depending on its cycle sizes is checked for every target through `n=5`. | **`KILL_SHALLOW_KERNEL_ENCODING`.** The update is just kernel partition followed by increasing-cycle notation, then collapse of every permutation to identity; both axes are static species bookkeeping. |
docs/papers172_176_sequence/scouting/fresh_geometry_automata/SCOUT_AND_KILL_LEDGER.md:14:| `D06_CRN` | Ordered distinct quadruples of `P^1(F_p)`.  Apply the unique projectivity sending the first three entries to `(infinity,0,1)`. | Full carriers for `p=3,5,7`; image/fixed count `p-2`, tail one. | Every canonical cross-ratio target has exactly `|PGL(2,p)|=p(p^2-1)` parents. | **`KILL_INTERNAL_AND_DIRECT`.** This is the projective-frame normalisation killed as P166 scout `F03`; triple transitivity and cross-ratio orbits are standard. |
docs/papers172_176_sequence/scouting/fresh_geometry_automata/SCOUT_AND_KILL_LEDGER.md:17:| `D09_ICC` | Permutations.  On each cycle support, replace its cyclic order by increasing cyclic order. | Every permutation through `S_8`; image/fixed size `Bell(n)`. | A canonical target with cycle supports `B` has `prod_B(|B|-1)!` parents. | **`KILL_CANONICAL_NOTATION`.** Increasing cycle notation is the update and the proof; no dynamical axis survives. |
docs/papers172_176_sequence/scouting/fresh_geometry_automata/SCOUT_AND_KILL_LEDGER.md:18:| `D10_BCA` | Accessible complete binary automata with fixed initial state zero.  Relabel states in alphabet-ordered BFS discovery order. | Every accessible transition table through `n=4` (31,488 at `n=4`); 5,248 canonical images there. | Every canonical target has exactly `(n-1)!` labelled parents because an accessible automorphism fixing the initial state and letters is trivial. | **`KILL_DIRECT_AUTOMATON_CANONICALISATION`.** BFS strings are the standard enumeration representation of initially connected DFAs. |
docs/papers172_176_sequence/scouting/fresh_geometry_automata/SCOUT_AND_KILL_LEDGER.md:19:| `D11_DLX` | Binary `r x c` matrices.  Sort rows lexicographically, then sort the resulting columns lexicographically, and repeat dynamically. | Complete boxes `2x2,2x3,3x3,3x4,4x4`.  Tails are `1,1,2,2,3`; all tested cycles are fixed; `4x4` has 650 fixed points and maximum fibre 576. | No uniform target reconstruction emerged. | **`KILL_DIRECT / NO ATLAS`.** Doubly lexical matrix ordering is directly owned; the growing clock is interesting but lacks an all-size theorem or independent fibre. |
docs/papers172_176_sequence/scouting/fresh_geometry_automata/SCOUT_AND_KILL_LEDGER.md:23:| `D15_LXP` | Labelled strict posets.  Output the total order given by the lexicographically least linear extension. | All labelled posets through `n=5` (4,231); image/fixed `n!`, maximum fibre 357 at `n=5`. | Exact target fibres are enumerated but do not factor target-locally. | **`KILL_ONE_STEP / NO INVERSE`.** Lexicographic topological sorting is the whole forward theorem and the second axis remains a coupled poset count. |
docs/papers172_176_sequence/scouting/fresh_geometry_automata/SCOUT_AND_KILL_LEDGER.md:26:| `D18_FCI` | Set partitions.  Conjugate the integer partition of block sizes and output the consecutive-interval partition of that new type. | Every partition through `n=9`; image size `p(n)`, recurrent fixed/2-cycles by self-conjugate types, all nonimage states at depth one. | A canonical target of type `mu` has `n!/(prod lambda_i! prod_s m_s(lambda)!)` parents for `lambda=mu'`. | **`KILL_QUOTIENT_SHADOW`.** This discards all labelled interlacing retained by `D01_ORT` and reduces to classical Ferrers conjugation plus a standard set-partition type count; P113 is the nearest occupied partition-diagram warning. |
