papers/64-lacunary-beta-entropy-approximants/sections/1_introduction.tex:3:The greedy $\beta$-expansion introduced by R\'enyi and characterized lexicographically by Parry turns the orbit of one into a complete symbolic boundary for the $\beta$-shift \cite{renyi_1957,parry_1960}.  When this expansion terminates, the boundary has a periodic quasi-greedy version and the associated shift is of finite type.  Truncating a nonterminating expansion therefore gives a natural route from a general $\beta$-shift to simple-Parry shifts.
