papers/64-lacunary-beta-entropy-approximants/sections/0_abstract.tex:2:We quantify the canonical simple-Parry approximation of a $\beta$-shift when the greedy expansion of one is binary and its zero gaps increase strictly.  The existence of such expansions and the qualitative truncation mechanism are already present in the $\beta$-expansion literature; our object is the entropy error.  If the ones occur at $n_1=1<n_2<\cdots$, if $\beta_j$ is defined by $\sum_{k\leq j}\beta_j^{-n_k}=1$, and if $L_j=\log\beta-\log\beta_j$, we prove a non-asymptotic two-sided certificate for $L_j$ and a fully finite rational root-enclosure version.  They yield the sharp law
